&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set a new pulse for healthcare!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join the &lt;strong&gt;DIAL&lt;/strong&gt; team in the &lt;strong&gt;Phone Assistant&lt;/strong&gt; domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission will be to design, build, and scale the AI-powered features that transform how practitioners and patients connect over the phone — making care more accessible for patients and reducing administrative burden for health professionals. You will work in a feature team developing the Phone Assistant, Doctolib&#39;s solution that combines LLM reasoning, speech recognition, and real-time backend systems, launching first in Germany and expanding to France and Italy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working in the tech team at Doctolib means building innovative products and features to improve the daily lives of care teams and patients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your responsibilities include but are not limited to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operate backend services in &lt;strong&gt;Node.js/TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt; (with Python exposure), designing for reliability, scalability, and real-time performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, evaluate, and ship &lt;strong&gt;LLM-based features&lt;/strong&gt; end-to-end: prompt engineering, tool calling, structured outputs, guardrails, and fallback strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own AI feature quality: build evaluation datasets and scorers (e.g., in Braintrust), track regressions, and make evidence-based ship decisions before each release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy and operate cloud-native services on &lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes&lt;/strong&gt; across major cloud providers (AWS/Azure/GCP), and evolve CI/CD pipelines with &lt;strong&gt;GitHub Actions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design data models and drive database migrations and performance tuning for real-time workloads (&lt;strong&gt;PostgreSQL&lt;/strong&gt;: connection pooling, indexing, query optimisation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high testing bar (unit, integration, e2e), debug distributed systems in production with strong observability, and contribute to pragmatic, secure architecture decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before you read on: if you don&#39;t have the exact profile described below, but you feel this job description matches your skill set, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be a great fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 5+ years of backend engineering experience building scalable, resilient systems in &lt;strong&gt;Node.js/TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt; (with some Python)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on production experience building LLM-based features: prompting, tool calling, structured outputs, eval frameworks, and handling real-world failure modes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have proven experience deploying and operating services on &lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes&lt;/strong&gt; within at least one major cloud provider (AWS, Azure, or GCP), with solid CI/CD practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strong testing culture (unit/integration/e2e), sharp debugging skills for microservices and distributed systems, and a focus on code quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are fluent in English, with a collaborative mindset and the drive to own problems end-to-end — from design to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It would be fantastic if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience with speech pipelines (ASR, TTS, streaming audio) or voice agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are familiar with event-driven architectures and message brokers (Kafka, RabbitMQ, NATS, or Redis Streams), and have hands-on PostgreSQL experience (EXPLAIN/ANALYZE, indexing strategies, connection pooling)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;H

